1116: ## 7. Integration with `window.SpatialNav`
1117: 
1118: The view controllers coordinate seamlessly with `window.SpatialNav` through standardized HTML data attributes, focus memory contracts, auto-scrolling margins, and focus trapping:
1119: 
1120: ### 7.1 Attribute Rules Matrix
1121: 
1122: | Attribute | Syntax | Required | Purpose |
1123: |---|---|---|---|
1124: | `data-nav` | `"true"` \| `"false"` | Yes | Dictates whether element participates in candidate discovery. |
1125: | `data-nav-group` | String (e.g. `shelf-trending-movies`) | Yes | Semantically groups elements for spatial memory and query filtering. |
1126: | `data-nav-index` | Integer String (`"0"`, `"1"`, ...) | Recommended | Defines ordinal sequence inside shelves and grids. Index 0 resets shelf scrollLeft. |
1127: | `data-nav-default`| `"true"` | Yes (1 per view) | Specifies primary default focus target when view memory is empty. |
1128: | `data-scroll-rail`| `"true"` | Optional | Marks container as horizontal shelf rail for auto-scroll tracking. |
1129: | `data-title` | String | Recommended | Used for fuzzy memory restoration if element is re-rendered with new ID. |
1130: 
1131: ### 7.2 Focus Memory Preservation During View Switching
1132: When transitioning between views (e.g. `Home -> Details -> Player -> Details -> Home`), `SpatialNav` implements a 6-tier resolution cascade:
1133: 1. Direct DOM node identity (`mem.element`)
1134: 2. Element ID (`mem.id`)
1135: 3. Group + Index (`[data-nav-group="..."][data-nav-index="..."]`)
1136: 4. Group + Title (`[data-nav-group="..."][data-title="..."]`)
1137: 5. View Default (`[data-nav-default="true"]`)
1138: 6. First navigable element in active view (`.view.active [data-nav="true"]`)
1139: 
1140: The view controllers hook into `CinejoyApp.switchView(targetView, data)`:
1141: ```javascript
1142: // In CinejoyApp.switchView:
1143: if (this.state.currentView && window.SpatialNav) {
1144:   window.SpatialNav.saveFocus(this.state.currentView);
1145: }
1146: 
1147: // ... activate new view ...
1148: 
1149: // Invoke view controller activate hook:
1150: if (targetView === 'home' && window.HomeViewController) {
1151:   window.HomeViewController.activate();
1152: } else if (targetView === 'movies' && window.MoviesViewController) {
1153:   window.MoviesViewController.activate();
1154: } else if (targetView === 'series' && window.SeriesViewController) {
1155:   window.SeriesViewController.activate();
1156: } else if (targetView === 'search' && window.SearchViewController) {
1157:   window.SearchViewController.activate();
1158: } else if (targetView === 'details' && window.DetailsViewController) {
1159:   window.DetailsViewController.activate(data);
1160: }
1161: 
1162: // Restore focus after DOM settling:
1163: window.SpatialNav.restoreFocus(targetView);
1164: ```
1165: 
1166: ### 7.3 Two-Tier TV-Safe Auto-Scroll Coordinates
1167: - **Horizontal Shelf Rail**:
1168:   - `SAFE_X_MIN`: `96px`
1169:   - `SAFE_X_MAX`: `1824px` (`1920 - 96`)
1170:   - `PEEK_OFFSET`: `48px`
1171:   - Rule: If `rect.left < 96px`, scrolls left by `96 - rect.left`. If `rect.right > 1824px`, scrolls right by `(rect.right - 1824) + 48`. Index 0 resets to `left: 0`.
1172: - **Vertical Viewport**:
1173:   - `EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN`: `104px` (84px fixed header + 20px buffer)
1174:   - `SAFE_Y_MAX`: `1026px` (`1080 - 54`)
1175:   - Rule: If shelf top < 104px, pane scrolls up. If card bottom > 1026px, pane scrolls down with 36px bottom buffer.
