1179: ## 8. Memory Management & Performance Constraints (1.5GB RAM webOS TV)
1180: 
1181: 1. **DocumentFragment Batching**: Never append cards individually in a loop. Always assemble cards in a `document.createDocumentFragment()` and append in a single DOM mutation.
1182: 2. **Shelf Item Capping**: Restrict horizontal shelves to a maximum of 20 elements. This bounds DOM nodes per shelf, keeping total view DOM count under ~150 elements.
1183: 3. **Lazy Image Loading & Local Fallbacks**:
1184:    - Every `<img>` tag specifies `loading="lazy"`.
1185:    - `onerror` handlers replace failed network images with inline SVG data URIs, eliminating 404 retry spam.
1186: 4. **Hardware Acceleration**:
1187:    - `[data-nav="true"]` has `transform: translateZ(0)` and `will-change: transform`.
1188:    - Card transitions execute purely on GPU (`transform: scale(1.08)`), avoiding layout reflows.
1189: 5. **Debounce Timers & In-Flight Cleanup**:
1190:    - Live multi-search debounces at 300ms.
1191:    - Any active debounce timer is cleared on view deactivation.
